    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499839/ctnerr-financial-assistant": {
      "title": "CTNERR Financial Assistant",
      "description": "UCONN - CTNERR Financial Assistant UCONN CTNERR Financial Assistant Job no: 499839 Position type: Part-time Location: UConn Avery Point Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Vice President for Research Department/Office: CT Ntl Estuarine Research Rsrv Categories: Fiscal, Accounting and Budget Apply now JOB SUMMARY Working under the supervision of the CT National Estuarine Research Reserve (CTNERR), the CTNERR Financial Assistant is a part-time position (50% FTE, 17.5 hours per week) that will help provide financial and program support for the administration and operation of the CT National Estuarine Research Reserve. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with creating and maintaining salary forecasts for CTNERR staff Schedule payroll authorizations (PAs) for submittal to UConn Payroll and maintain PA records Organize and track grant related cost-transfer requests Create and maintain grant award effort reporting/commitment changes Assist in generating grant-related financial reports and assembling data for distribution to CTNERR staff and others Perform other related work as assigned (e.g., inventory control, purchasing assistance, etc.) MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Associate’s degree in a financial field and at least two years of related experience with payroll and financial tracking and reporting; OR an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated experience using Microsoft Office software (specifically Excel) or similar spreadsheet software. Experience with state or federal grant funding. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in financial field. Experience interpreting and applying grant policies and procedures. Experience working in a college, university, or public service role. Knowledge of National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) or US Environmental Protection Agency (US EPA) grant funding programs. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a part-time, end-dated position with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and funding. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. This position is based at the Avery Point campus. The full-time, annualized salary range is $56,000 to $62,000 (prorated to $28,000 to $31,000 for 50% appointment). Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499839 to upload a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 6, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 22 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Oct 06 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Oct 06 2026 CTNERR Financial Assistant in UConn Avery Point The CT National Estuarine Research Reserve (CTNERR) Financial Assistant is a part-time position that will help provide financial and program support for the administration and operation of the CTNERR. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/498966/custodian": {
      "title": "UCONN",
      "description": "UCONN - Custodian UCONN Custodian Job no: 498966 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: President School/Unit: Student Life and Enrollment (AVP of Student Life) Department/Office: Student Union Categories: Custodial Apply now Custodian Salary Range: $43,301.00-$54,108.00 Yearly Individuals new to state service start at the minimum of the pay plan. Link to Custodian Job Specification: https://www.jobapscloud.com/CT/specs/classspecdisplay.asp?ClassNumber=0429TC&R1=&R3= THIS POSITION IS OPEN TO CURRENT UCONN EMPLOYEES ONLY INTRODUCTION The State of Connecticut, University of Connecticut’s Student Union department has one Custodian job opening at the Storrs Campus. This is a permanent, full-time, 37.5 hours/week position. The starting hourly salary is $22.13/hour and is non-negotiable. Working under the supervision of the Lead Custodian, Supervising Custodian, or Building Services Manager, the successful candidate will be accountable for performing a full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of the Student Union building. Below is the current shift and work schedule: 3rd shift, 11:00 PM–7:00 AM, Sunday-Thursday This position is categorized as Emergency Support Services/Essential Staff.  The individual in this role must be willing to work during emergency closures/delayed openings due to inclement weather or for significant events that effect campus operations.  Applicants must also be willing to respond to emergencies on overtime (nights, weekends, holidays). SELECTION PLAN In order to be considered for this job opening, you must meet the minimum qualifications as listed on the job opening and must specify your qualifications on your application. Applications will be evaluated to ensure that the Knowledge, Skill and Ability, Minimum Qualifications and Special Requirement sections of the position have been met. Ensure that your PageUp Application is complete and detailed before submitting it. You will not be able to make revisions once your application is submitted.  Although it is not required, applicants are strongly encouraged to submit a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional, work-related references along with their contact information. At any point of the recruitment process, applicants may be contacted via email and provided an opportunity to submit addition documentation which supports their qualification(s) for this position.  These documents may include: a cover letter, resume, performance reviews, attendance records, supervisory references, licensure, etc., at the discretion of the hiring department.  Applicants must meet the minimum qualifications and special requirements, as indicated, to apply for this position. If selected for an interview, you will be asked to provide the names, titles and phone numbers of three professional references.  In addition, current State of Connecticut employee applicants at UConn or other State Agencies, may be asked to provide copies of their last two (2) performance appraisals and their CORE attendance records.  Employment will be contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment physical examination, including drug testing, as well as a criminal background check. Please regularly check your email provided on your application for notifications. Please check your SPAM and/or Junk folders on a daily basis in the event an email provider auto-notification emails in a user's spam. PURPOSES OF JOB CLASS (NATURE OF WORK) Is accountable for performing the full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of the Student Union building and other buildings under the responsibility of the Student Union and Event Services department. EXAMPLES OF DUTIES Performs custodial tasks and maintenance of such areas as administrative offices, meeting and function rooms, lounges, theatre, restrooms, lobby areas and outdoor areas in and around the Student Union building and other buildings under the responsibility of the Student Union. Dusts, mops, sweeps, scrubs, strips, waxes, and polishes floors using appropriate equipment, such as buffers, scrubbers and extractors. Washes, dusts, and polishes glass including windows, woodwork and walls, furniture and metal equipment. Collects and disposes of trash and performs recycling as instructed. Provides a report of equipment in need of repair, performs minor maintenance, run errands, inspects building for damage and reports conditions to a supervisor for action. May change light bulbs, lubricate door hinges, drawers or cabinets, etc. Remove snow and ice from stairways and walkways applying sand and salt as needed around the Student Union building. Move furniture and/or set-up meeting rooms for events. Performs other duties are required. KNOWLEDGE, SKILL, AND ABILITY Skills interpersonal skills; oral and written communication skills; Ability to follow oral and written instructions; operate, care for and perform minor maintenance on tools and equipment used in daily work; keep records. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Any experience and training which would provide the knowledge, skills and abilities listed above. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS A minimum of three years of custodial experience. Custodial experience in an educational setting. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Incumbent in this class must have adequate strength, stamina, physical agility and visual and auditory acuity, and must maintain such physical fitness as to be able to perform the duties of the class. A physical examination is required. WORKING CONDITIONS Incumbent in this class may be required to lift moderate to heavy weights and may be exposed to risk of injury from equipment and/or individuals. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check and pre-employment physical. APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #498966. Although it is not required, applicants are strongly encouraged to submit a resume , cover letter , and a list of three professional, work-related references along with their contact information. This job posting is anticipated to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 2, 2026. CONCLUSION All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . Information concerning the University’s policies regarding the Cleary Act Statement, Non-Discrimination Policy, Accommodations for Applicants with Disabilities, and Recruiting Veterans can be found on UConn’s Job page. Please review the required notices and policy statements . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 18 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Oct 02 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Oct 02 2026 Custodian in UConn Storrs The State of Connecticut, University of Connecticut’s Student Union and Event Services department has one custodial job opening at the Storrs Campus that is 3rd shift, 11:00 PM–7:00 AM, Sunday-Thursday. Working under the supervision of the Lead Custodian, Supervising Custodian, or Building Services Manager, the successful candidate will be accountable for performing a full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of the Student Union building. Open to current UConn employees only. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499620/equine-care-specialist-animal-care-specialist-2-positions": {
      "title": "Equine Care Specialist (Animal Care Specialist)",
      "description": "UCONN - Equine Care Specialist (Animal Care Specialist) - 2 positions UCONN Equine Care Specialist (Animal Care Specialist) - 2 positions Job no: 499620 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Agriculture,Health,Natural Rcs Department/Office: Animal Science Categories: Health and Safety, Laboratory and Research Operations Apply now JOB SUMMARY The Department of Animal Science, a part of the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, within the University of Connecticut, seeks qualified applicants for two (2) full-time positions of Equine Care Specialist (Animal Care Specialist). The Equine Care Specialist is responsible for feeding, watering, grooming, handling, and monitoring horses; maintaining barns, paddocks, arenas, and related facilities; assisting with veterinary and farrier care; operating farm equipment; and supporting instructional and experiential learning opportunities for students. These positions play a critical role in ensuring the health and welfare of University-owned horses while maintaining a safe, efficient, and well-organized equine operation. The successful candidates will play a key role in supporting the daily operation of the Horse Unit and assisting in the continued growth and success of the Department's Animal Science as well as Equine Science and Management programs. Through the provision of high-quality equine care, facility support, and student engagement, these positions will contribute to the unit's teaching, research, and outreach mission. The positions will supervise student employees and may supervise temporary staff as assigned. The Equine Care Specialists will report to the Horse Unit Manager and the Department Head of Animal Science and will be based on the University of Connecticut’s Storrs Campus. About The Horse Unit and Equine Programs The UConn Horse Unit is a cornerstone of the Department of Animal Science's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Housing approximately 70 horses across two facilities, the Horse Unit supports a wide range of academic instruction, research activities, extension programs, and equine management operations. Facilities include horse barns, tack rooms, classrooms, laboratories, training areas, and a lighted outdoor arena. The Horse Unit serves as the hands-on learning center for UConn's Equine Science and Management program, which prepares students for careers throughout the equine industry through a combination of classroom instruction, applied learning experiences, and direct engagement with horse care and management. The program integrates science-based coursework with practical training in equine health, behavior, nutrition, reproduction, facility management, and industry operations. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITES Equine Care and Husbandry Provide daily care for horses, including feeding, watering, grooming, turnout, blanketing, exercising, and monitoring overall health and well-being. Observe horses for signs of illness, injury, behavioral concerns, or other health-related issues and promptly communicate concerns to appropriate personnel. Assist with routine veterinary, farrier, reproductive, and other animal health procedures as needed. Administer medications and treatments in accordance with established protocols and training. Maintain accurate health, treatment, and animal management records. Facility Operations and Maintenance Clean, maintain, and prepare stalls, barns, paddocks, arenas, and other Horse Unit facilities to support safe and effective operations. Assist with providing feed, hay, bedding for animals;  manure, ; and supply management including receiving, storing, monitoring, and maintaining inventory levels. Operate and perform routine maintenance on tractors, utility vehicles, farm equipment, and related tools. Identify and report facility, equipment, and safety concerns and assist with corrective actions as appropriate. Teaching, Student Support, and Outreach Support teaching, research, outreach, extension, and experiential learning activities conducted through the Horse Unit. Train and supervise student employees in horse care, facility operations, animal handling, and established safety procedures. Assist with student learning activities, demonstrations, clinics, competitions, tours, and outreach programs hosted by the Department and Horse Unit. May supervise temporary employees and volunteers as assigned. Administrative and Compliance Responsibilities Maintain records related to animal care, inventories, equipment maintenance, and operational activities. Assist with compliance with University and  departmental animal care and safety requirements. Participate in required trainings and support adherence to established animal welfare and workplace safety standards. Perform related duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in Animal Science, Equine Science, Agricultural Science, Biology, or a related field and two (2) to three (3) years of related animal care experience; OR Associate's degree in Animal Science, Equine Science, Agricultural Science, Biology, or a related field and four (4) to five (5) years of related animal care experience; OR an equivalent combination of education and related experience. Experience handling and caring for horses in an equine, agricultural, research, educational, or comparable setting. Demonstrated experience working independently and collaboratively in a team environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working in an equine teaching, research, extension, or boarding facility. Experience operating tractors, utility vehicles, and other farm equipment. Experience training or supervising student employees, volunteers, or temporary staff. Experience assisting with veterinary, farrier, or reproductive management activities. Experience maintaining animal health, treatment, or operational records. APPOINTMENT TERMS These are 12-month, full-time, end-dated, UCPEA positions working 35 hours per week. The anticipated start date is October 2026, but may be subject to change. These positions are funded for an initial one-year term, with the possibility of renewal based on performance, operational needs, and the availability of funding. These positions are located on the main University of Connecticut campus in Storrs, CT. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. Salary will be commensurate with the successful candidates’ background and work experience. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of successful candidates is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check and a pre-employment physical. The successful incumbents must have the ability to safely handle horses and perform physically demanding work; to work indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions; to operate farm equipment and related tools safely; to work weekends, holidays, and other non-standard hours as needed to support animal care operations; and to follow established animal care and safety protocols. These positions are categorized as Emergency Support Services (Essential Employees).  Individuals in these roles must be willing to work during emergency closures/delayed openings due to inclement weather or for significant events that affect campus operations; applicants must also be willing to respond to emergencies including nights/weekends/holidays. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499620 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. Evaluations of applications will begin immediately and continue until filled. For questions regarding this position, you may reach out to Dr. Sarah Reed. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 2, 2026 All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 18 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Oct 02 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Oct 02 2026 Equine Care Specialist (Animal Care Specialist) - 2 positions in UConn Storrs The Department of Animal Science, a part of the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, within the University of Connecticut, seeks qualified applicants for two (2) full-time positions of Equine Care Specialist (Animal Care Specialist). The Equine Care Specialist is responsible for feeding, watering, grooming, handling, and monitoring horses; maintaining barns, paddocks, arenas, and related facilities; assisting with veterinary and farrier care; operating farm equipment; and supporting instructional and experiential learning opportunities for students. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499225/clinical-veterinarian": {
      "title": "UCONN",
      "description": "UCONN - Clinical Veterinarian UCONN Clinical Veterinarian Job no: 499225 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Vice President for Research (Research Integrity) Department/Office: Research Integrity (Vice President for Research) Categories: Executive Apply now JOB SUMMARY This full-time Clinical Veterinarian position is primarily clinical, providing veterinary care and veterinary services in support of the organization’s research mission. The Clinical Veterinarian will provide daily support to diagnose, treat, and manage clinical cases identified in the research colonies; assist with disease surveillance and prevention programs; participate in various activities to ensure compliance with regulations and guidelines; and assist the Director with administration and management of the animal care and use program. In addition, the successful candidate will provide professional service primarily in the areas of anesthesia and surgery and will oversee post-operative care of animals in support of specific research programs. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provides direct veterinary care. Consults with and instructs investigators on the diagnosis and treatment of animals; preventive health programs; selection of animal models; selection and administration of anesthetics, analgesics, and tranquilizers; and planning and conduct of animal surgical procedures. Assists in development of training programs and participates in training of individuals who work with animals to meet regulatory and accreditation requirements. Manages preventive health programs. Advises and mentors support staff to foster their understanding of their role in animal care program processes. Collaborates with administrators, faculty, animal care staff, and the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) to evaluate facilities and practices and to recommend practical and effective animal care and use procedures and maintenance systems. Provides veterinary pre-review of IACUC protocols. May serve as a voting member of the IACUC. Provide cross-campus support for UConn Health, UConn Storrs, and UConn regional campuses as needed. Perform other related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (VMD/DVM) Degree from an American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or Educational Commission for Foreign Veterinary Graduates (ECFVG) certificate and license to practice veterinary medicine in at least one state in the United States, with ability to obtain CT licensure upon hire. Possession of, or the ability to obtain within 12 months of hire, controlled substance licensure in the State of Connecticut. Board certification/eligibility in laboratory animal medicine or 3-5 years of relevant private practice experience (e.g., exotic and small animal practice). Demonstrated oral and written communication skills, with a proven track record of leading presentations. Demonstrated experience utilizing analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills with an aptitude for detailed work. Experience with computer software applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.). PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS USDA-accredited veterinarian. Evidence of completion of advanced training in laboratory animal medicine; veterinary anesthesiology, surgery or emergency medicine; or other relevant veterinary specialties. Experience working with agricultural and/or wildlife species in research, husbandry, or field settings is a plus. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. For additional information regarding benefits, please visit UConn Health Benefits and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. An annual vaccination against influenza is required. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499225 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. Screening will begin immediately, and the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found.  Priority will be given to applications received by 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 19, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Nov 19 2026 Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Nov 19 2026 Clinical Veterinarian in UConn Storrs This full-time position is primarily clinical, providing veterinary care and veterinary services in support of the organization’s research mission. The Clinical Veterinarian will provide daily support to diagnose, treat, and manage clinical cases identified in the research colonies; assist with disease surveillance and prevention programs; participate in various activities to ensure compliance with regulations and guidelines; and assist the Director with administration and management of the animal care and use program. In addition, the successful candidate will provide professional service primarily in the areas of anesthesia and surgery and will oversee post-operative care of animals in support of specific research programs. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
