    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499840/research-associate-or-postdoctoral-research-associate-fabris-group": {
      "title": "Research Associate or Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fabris Group)",
      "description": "UCONN - Research Associate or Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fabris Group) UCONN Research Associate or Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fabris Group) Job no: 499840 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Physical Sciences) Department/Office: Chemistry Categories: Postdoctoral Research Associates Apply now JOB SUMMARY The Laboratory of Dr. Dan Fabris in the Chemistry Department at the University of Connecticut, Storrs, is seeking a Research Associate/Post-Doctoral Fellow to participate in Epitranscriptomics projects aimed at investigating the functional roles of RNA post-transcriptional modifications (rPTMs) in the cell response to viral infections and other types of stresses. Highly motivated individuals holding a PhD in the Life Sciences or an M.S. degree with extensive experience are encouraged to apply. This position will be hired at either the Postdoctoral Research Associate classification or the Research Associate 1 classification, dependent upon the incumbent's experience, skills, and abilities as determined by the University. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES The Postdoctoral Research Associate or Research Associate will be responsible for the following tasks: Conduct research aimed at elucidating the dynamics of rPTMs in human cell cultures infected with HIV-1 and hepatitis C. Generate and maintain cultures in which the genes for selected rPTM writers, erasers, and readers have been effectively knocked out. Perform proper control experiments by using a variety of biochemical, spectroscopic and electrophoretic techniques. Purify viral and host RNA for advanced mass spectrometric analysis. Optimize and troubleshoot current experimental procedures. Train and lead a team of undergraduate and graduate research assistants Postdoctoral Research Associates will be responsible for these additional tasks: Participate in designing experiments and completing data analysis and interpretation. Write publications; participate in dissemination. The incumbent will be expected to use initiative in the planning and execution of the different tasks; to maintain the research productivity necessary to cultivate a presence in the scientific community; to develop a good understanding of how to best prioritize the various tasks according to the situation on the ground; to maintain the maximum possible flexibility to facilitate the solution of unforeseen problems. No direct experience is required in mass spectrometry and related techniques. If necessary, appropriate training will be provided to the new hire. The incumbent will report directly to Dr. Fabris, the laboratory’s principal investigator. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Postdoctoral Research Associate: PhD in Chemistry or a closely related field. Research Associate 1: PhD in Chemistry or a closely related field and no experience to one year of post-degree experience; or an M.A. or M.S. in Chemistry or a closely related field, and eight to ten years of post-degree experience. Experience in virology, cell biology, and gene silencing techniques. RNA biochemistry, molecular biology, and pertinent bioassays. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) techniques. Experience with next-generation sequencing (NGS) techniques. APPOINTMENT TERMS The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and accumulated experience. The start date for the position is anticipated for November 2026. The position is for an initial one-year appointment and is potentially renewable for a second year upon mutual agreement, funding availability, and performance. Continuation beyond two years is contingent upon future external funding applications. Postdoctoral Research Associate - Other rights and terms and conditions of your appointment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace, and Agricultural Implement Workers of America (UAW), Local 6950; Research Associate 1 - Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the American Association of University Professors UConn Chapter (AAUP). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499840 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 26, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Oct 26 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Oct 26 2026 Research Associate or Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fabris Group) in UConn Storrs The Laboratory of Dr. Dan Fabris in the Chemistry Department at the University of Connecticut, Storrs, is seeking a Research Associate/Post-Doctoral Fellow to participate in Epitranscriptomics projects aimed at investigating the functional roles of RNA post-transcriptional modifications (rPTMs) in the cell response to viral infections and other types of stresses. Highly motivated individuals holding a PhD in the Life Sciences or an M.S. degree with extensive experience are encouraged to apply. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499856/research-associate-rural-health": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Rural Health)",
      "description": "UCONN - Research Associate (Rural Health) UCONN Research Associate (Rural Health) Job no: 499856 Position type: Full-time Location: Other - please see posting for additional information Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Social Work Department/Office: Innovations Institute Categories: Research Apply now JOB SUMMARY The Innovations Institute at the University of Connecticut School of Social Work seeks a Research Associate 1 to support the evaluation of the Connecticut Rural Health Transformation Program (CT RHTP), a five-year, statewide initiative funded by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) and administered by the Connecticut Department of Social Services. The evaluation team is responsible for developing and implementing an overarching framework to measure implementation, outcomes, and sustainability across 30 projects spanning four initiative areas: Population Health, Workforce, Data and Technology, and Care Transformation and Stability. Positions with the Innovations Institute are fully remote, with expected travel to UConn's Hartford Campus twice annually. The Research Associate 1 will work with the project Principal Investigator and Co-Directors to contribute methodological and analytic expertise across the CT RHTP evaluation and will report to the Principal Investigator. This includes assisting with facilitating, and when appropriate, leading the design of research and evaluation plans, conducting quantitative and mixed-methods analyses, translating findings into products for diverse audiences, and providing technical assistance to project teams, state agencies, and community partners. The Research Associate 1 will also contribute to cross-project learning and continuous quality improvement, co-author academic and public-facing products, and help ensure that data security, privacy, and compliance requirements are met across all participating entities. This position also requires project management, including communicating with project staff and external partners, facilitating meetings, and coordinating and aligning efforts across projects and initiatives. This position is well suited to a doctoral-level researcher with training and experience in health services research, program evaluation, and implementation science, and a strong interest in improving healthcare access and outcomes in rural communities. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with, facilitate, and co-lead the design and development of research and evaluation plans, including study design, sampling, measurement, data collection procedures, and analytic strategy across assigned projects. Work directly with stakeholders and project teams to identify research and evaluation needs and translate them into rigorous, feasible study designs that support continuous quality improvement (CQI) and evaluation goals. Assist with, facilitate, and co-lead quantitative and mixed-methods analytic plans, applying appropriate statistical methods and interpreting findings to generate actionable insights. Manage complex data sets and primary data using statistical software (e.g., Excel, SPSS, SAS, R, STATA), and establish processes to ensure data quality, accuracy, and analysis readiness. Conduct literature reviews and synthesize evidence to inform study design, contextualize findings, and support evidence-based recommendations. Provide technical assistance to service providers and public agencies in developing data collection procedures, building instruments, reviewing data, and resolving data quality issues. Develop data visualizations tailored to internal and external stakeholders that clearly communicate complex findings. Facilitate the preparation and management of Data Use Agreements (DUAs), IRB submissions, and related compliance documentation. Independently write and co-author products, including academic manuscripts, public-facing one-pagers, and technical reports for decision-makers. Supervise, mentor, and provide guidance to graduate students and other research staff on data collection, analysis, storage, and reporting, and review their work for quality and accuracy. Serve as a subject-matter expert in program evaluation, implementation science, and quantitative data analysis for internal and external partners. Assist with the Rural Health Evaluation Advisory Board and the evaluators' Community of Practice (CoP). Coordinate and facilitate internal and external communications and meetings. Co-author manuscripts in peer-reviewed journals and present findings at academic and professional conferences. Contribute to the development and writing of federal, state, and private grant proposals. Contribute to and manage work plans, ensuring milestones and reporting deadlines are met. Perform other duties as needed. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in Social Sciences, Social Work, Education, Public Policy, Public Health, Health Science, Statistics, Economics, or another field of study related to research. Demonstrated ability to develop and maintain relevant subject-matter knowledge related to rural health, health services, program evaluation, and the RHTP initiative areas. Experience performing literature reviews and presenting results. Demonstrated knowledge of research study design and data collection procedures, and the ability to understand and use scientific terminology and research theory. Demonstrated knowledge of regulations governing the confidentiality of subjects and the ability to maintain the confidentiality of information obtained. Evidence of skill in statistical programming, data and statistical analysis, and interpreting findings using statistical software (e.g., SPSS, SAS, R, STATA). Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects at once, respond to tight timelines, pay close attention to detail, and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Social Sciences, Social Work, Education, Public Policy, Public Health, Health Science, Statistics, Economics, or another field of study related to research. Experience developing and maintaining effective working relationships with partners, including funders, internal colleagues, and other stakeholders, and partnering with diverse stakeholders to develop research agendas related to outcomes, feedback, and evaluations. Demonstrated skill in using measurable and verifiable information for making decisions and judgments. Experience supervising or mentoring graduate students, trainees, or junior research staff in a research or evaluation setting. Demonstrated knowledge of implementation science, rapid-cycle evaluation, and data visualization. Experience supervising other analysts, including drafting evaluation plans. Demonstrated ability to convey complex information clearly, in writing and orally, so that it is easily understood by stakeholders and organizations. Stated willingness to learn and effectively use new technology, maintaining productivity and using strategies to increase knowledge base. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, end-dated position with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and available funding. Positions with the Innovations Institute are fully remote and expected to travel to UConn's Hartford Campus once a year at the employee's expense. Candidates who reside in Connecticut to engage in in-person project activities are preferred. The salary range for this position is $85,000 to $111,000, commensurate with education and experience. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. For additional information regarding benefits, please visit UConn Health Benefits and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers.  Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the American Association of University Professors (AAUP). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499856 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on December 1, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 02 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Dec 01 2026 Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search."
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499868/postdoctoral-research-associate": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "UCONN - Postdoctoral Research Associate UCONN Postdoctoral Research Associate Job no: 499868 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Physical Sciences) Department/Office: Geog, Sustain, Comm Urban Stds Categories: Postdoctoral Research Associates Apply now JOB SUMMARY The Species Interactions & Global Change Research Group at the University of Connecticut invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Associate to join the group and contribute to an interdisciplinary research program at the intersection of biological invasions, ecology, and artificial intelligence (AI). DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will develop and apply AI approaches to improve prediction of biological invasions across species, ecosystems, and geographic regions. The project will emphasize the development and evaluation of probabilistic and interpretable machine-learning models, including approaches for uncertainty quantification, model calibration, and transferability. The Postdoc will also contribute to the development of reproducible computational workflows and tools that can support ecological forecasting and invasion-risk assessment. The Postdoc will work under the mentorship of Dr. Julissa Rojas-Sandoval and collaborate with an interdisciplinary network of researchers in invasion ecology, data science, and AI. The position offers considerable opportunity for intellectual independence, development of new research directions, publication of high-impact papers, participation in international collaborations, and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate researchers. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Ecology, Environmental Science, Computational Biology, Bioinformatics, Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, Geography, or a closely related field, completed by the start date. Research experience analyzing ecological, biodiversity, or environmental datasets. Demonstrated quantitative and computational skills. Experience conducting independent research and contributing to peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated written and oral communication, and collaborative skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Programming skills in Python and/or R, including experience developing reproducible and well-documented analytical workflows. Experience applying machine learning and/or advanced statistical modeling to ecological, environmental, or biological questions. Experience with probabilistic ML, interpretable AI, uncertainty quantification, model calibration, transfer learning, domain adaptation, causal inference, or ensemble modeling. Experience with large datasets, spatial analysis, GIS, and integrating multiple ecological data sources. Experience with reproducible research, version control, or high-performance/cloud computing. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, 12-month Postdoctoral Research Associate position at the University of Connecticut. The position may be renewed annually based on satisfactory performance and availability of funds for up to 2 years. Salary and benefits will be commensurate with University guidelines and the applicable collective bargaining agreement.  Other rights and terms and conditions of your appointment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace, and Agricultural Implement Workers of America (UAW), Local 6950. The preferred start date is early in the Spring 2027 semester , although some flexibility may be possible. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499868 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 02 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Postdoctoral Research Associate in UConn Storrs The Species Interactions & Global Change Research Group at the University of Connecticut invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Associate to join the group and contribute to an interdisciplinary research program at the intersection of biological invasions, ecology, and artificial intelligence (AI). Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499118/supplier-engagement-program-manager": {
      "title": "UCONN",
      "description": "UCONN - Supplier Engagement Program Manager UCONN Supplier Engagement Program Manager Job no: 499118 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: Chief Financial Officer School/Unit: Procurement Department/Office: Procurement Categories: Administrative Services Apply now JOB SUMMARY The University’s Procurement team is seeking a mission-driven Supplier Engagement Program Manager who is committed to expanding opportunities for Connecticut suppliers and building meaningful connections between the University and the businesses that serve Connecticut. The successful candidate will play a key role in strengthening UConn’s supplier engagement strategy, increasing participation among Connecticut-based businesses, and helping suppliers navigate opportunities with UConn. This position manages and supervises all administrative services for the University Supplier Engagement Program (USEP) and is accountable for performing and managing the most complex tasks within the USEP.  Responsibilities include but are not limited to leading the development and implementation of the University and UConn Heath’s (UCH) vendor engagement strategy and supervising activities, reports, and processes of a team serving the University’s main campus in Storrs, all regional campuses, and UConn Health in Farmington. This position is located at the main campus in Storrs, CT but requires a flexible schedule and regular in-state travel to conduct training, outreach and attend meetings and events. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBIBLITIES Responsible for the effectiveness of all University and UCH supplier engagement programs. Directs the day-to-day operation and administration of USEP, and assists in the planning, direction, coordination and expansion of USEP. Works collaboratively with various offices within the University and UCH and serves as an advisor to university administrators, staff, business leaders and/or other constituents regarding policies, procedures, statutory requirements and reporting responsibilities specific to USEP. Serves as USEP liaison to Department of Administrative Services and the Commission on Human Rights with regard to developing and executing complex supplier diversity strategies to increase participation and meet statutory goals. Performs office management duties for USEP; prepares comprehensive analyses, reports and recommendations for administrative decision-making; and supervises, trains and evaluates assigned personnel. Plans, organizes and administers workshops and training programs, in accordance with program goals.  Represents the University and UCH in key supplier engagement related organizations, committees and conferences. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Business or related field and a minimum of five (5) years professional experience in procurement of materials/commodities in a comparable environment OR an Associate’s degree in a closely related field and seven (7) or more years of related professional experience in a comparable environment, OR an equivalency of education and relevant experience which includes at least nine (9) years’ professional experience in procurement of materials/commodities in a comparable environment. Experience in supplier relationship management, including oversight of performance and compliance. Strong leadership, supervisory, organizational, project management, and planning skills with the ability to meet deadlines and facilitate solutions in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge of and experience in negotiating, administering and supervising procurement and business-related activities. General knowledge of supplier engagement principles, laws, regulations and applicable federal and state procurement statutes and policies. Ability to develop and implement supplier engagement and other supplier related strategies and activities. Ability to identify and resolve complex issues efficiently, effectively and independently. Strong interpersonal and persuasiveness skills and the ability to work effectively with all levels of employees and management. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position located at the Storrs campus. The department is currently working under a hybrid model requiring staff to be on the Storrs campus two (2) days per week and to work remotely three (3) days per week. The hybrid work schedule may change subject to authorization and University policy. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. The annual salary will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s background and experience. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT This position requires regular travel. Successful candidate must have dependable transportation and must be willing and able to work occasional evenings and weekends. Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499118 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . References will not be contacted without prior notice to the successful candidate(s). Screening will begin immediately. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 30, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Oct 30 2026 Supplier Engagement Program Manager in UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut's Procurement team is seeking a mission-driven individual who is committed to expanding opportunities for Connecticut suppliers and building meaningful connections between the University and the businesses that serve Connecticut. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499450/contract-specialist-1": {
      "title": "Contract Specialist 1",
      "description": "UCONN - Contract Specialist 1 UCONN Contract Specialist 1 Job no: 499450 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: Chief Financial Officer School/Unit: Procurement Department/Office: Procurement Categories: Grants and Contracts Apply now JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut seeks to hire a Contract Specialist to support the Procurement Contracting & Compliance team with a variety of contracts in support of the needs of the campus community.  Under the general direction of the University Director of Procurement Contracting & Compliance and/or the Senior Contract Specialist, this role will utilize existing policies, procedures, and statutes to draft and negotiate terms and conditions for a variety of university contracts. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include but are not limited to: Drafts and negotiates contract language for various contracts under assigned commodities. Responsible for the administration of all contractual activities for University Procurement Contracting & Compliance, as they relate to the needs of the University community. Collaborate with internal customer departments and colleagues within Procurement, as needed, to draft clear contracts that accurately capture the negotiated business terms. Represents the department with authority to act on behalf of the University Director, when expressly authorized. Ensures proper controls over contracting procedures for sound fiscal and administrative management and compliance with state ethics codes. Responsible for preparation and legal review of contracts and agreements submitted to the Office of the General Counsel and Office of the Attorney General. Monitors and tracks contracts and related documents for compliance with State and Federal statutes, Board of Trustees policies, Office of the General Counsel/Attorney General guidelines, internal procedures formulated by the University, and contract terms and conditions. Prepares and manages reports; maintains knowledge of, and interprets, applicable State and Federal statutes and regulations, Board of Trustees policies, Office of the General Counsel/Attorney General Guidelines, and the State’s Code of Ethics; provides information, instruction and/or training, as needed or requested, in relation to university compliance with contractual matters. Inform customers and/or vendors on new and/or current procurement procedures and guidelines. Analyzes technical data, i.e., scope of work and pricing information, vendor performance, and compliance with finalizing contracts. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in business, or a related field and four years of related professional experience in a comparable environment OR an Associate’s degree in business, or a related field and six years of related professional experience in a comparable environment OR eight years of professional contracting experience in a comparable environment. General working knowledge of accepted procurement practices and the ability to negotiate contract language to address the risks related to each type of arrangement which may be used in a wide range of varying and unique commodity groups and/or services. Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills. Excellent computer skills with strong technical skills to work with multiple software programs including Microsoft Office. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision under tight deadlines while managing multiple projects. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s or advanced degree in related discipline. Knowledge of contract theory, principles, laws, regulations and applicable federal and state procurement statutes, and policies. Experience developing and executing complex contracting strategies that maximize workflow efficiencies, process improvements, and operational performance. Experience with contracting in the State of Connecticut. Ability to assess organizational needs, communicate those needs to the vendor community, negotiate as needed, and evaluate contracts to determine technical compliance and resolve discrepancies. Knowledge of contract management systems automated procurement systems (e.g., Jaggaer). APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time position at the Storrs campus working Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. The starting salary range for this position will be $75,000-$83,727 and final salary will be determined based on the successful candidate’s experience and training. The department is currently working under a hybrid work schedule requiring all staff to be on the Storrs campus two (2) days per week and working remotely three (3) days per week.  This schedule may change subject to authorization and University policy. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499450 to upload a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three (3) professional references. References will not be contacted without prior notice to the successful candidate(s). Screening will begin immediately. For detailed information about this position and the department, please visit our website . This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 16, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Oct 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Oct 16 2026 Contract Specialist 1 in UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut seeks to hire a Contract Specialist to support the Procurement Contracting & Compliance team with a variety of contracts in support of the needs of the campus community.  Under the general direction of the University Director of Procurement Contracting & Compliance and/or the Senior Contract Specialist, this role will utilize existing policies, procedures, and statutes to draft and negotiate terms and conditions for a variety of University contracts. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499671/visiting-assistant-extension-educator-in-land-use": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use",
      "description": "UCONN - Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use UCONN Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use Job no: 499671 Position type: Full-time Location: Middlesex County Extension Ctr Division/Equivalent: Provost Academic Affairs School/Unit: Agriculture,Health,Natural Rcs Department/Office: Dept of Extension Middlesex (Department of Extension) Categories: Faculty Extension Educator Apply now INTRODUCTION We seek an individual whose professional skills and abilities can provide statewide outreach and training to land use commissioners and others on issues related to land use planning and decision making. This position (Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use) will lead the award-winning Land Use Academy in the Center for Land Use Education and Research , advance the Center’s mission of supporting communities in balancing growth and natural resource protection, and have the opportunity to contribute to efforts to connect undergraduates with community extension work. The ideal candidate will have professional, municipal-level experience in land use planning, an understanding of community resilience in extreme weather events, and experience in outreach or teaching on these topics. This non-tenure track faculty level position reports to the Head of the Department of Extension, College of Agriculture and Natural Resources. The Department of Extension in the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources works collaboratively with partners in all 169 municipalities across Connecticut, throughout the northeast region and beyond. It is a non-tenuring unit with 35 faculty, 30 program and administrative staff. Additional grant-specific program personnel assist to solve problems and enhance the wellbeing of our state citizens where they live, work, and learn. Work carried out by the department constitutes much of the UConn Extension System. Faculty and staff conduct activities through eight county/community-based offices and may be co-located with additional community/agency based working partners when applicable. The University serves as a beacon of academic and research excellence as well as a center for innovation and social service to communities. The University and CAHNR prioritize scholarship in areas that impact quality of life, including human, animal, plant and environmental health and sustainability. We encourage and provide support for cross-disciplinary, collaborative scholarship across the College, University, nation, and globe. UConn is committed to Life Transforming Education for students and Extension audiences. UConn is recognized as one of the most sustainable and environmentally friendly campuses by the Sierra Club. Through research, teaching, service, and Extension, UConn embraces diversity and inclusion, and cultivates leadership, integrity, and engaged citizenship in its students, faculty, staff, and alumni. Founded in 1881, UConn is a Land Grant and Sea Grant institution and member of the Space Grant Consortium. It is the state’s flagship institution of higher education and includes a main campus in Storrs, CT, four regional campuses throughout the state, and 13 Schools and Colleges, including a Law School in Hartford and Medical and Dental Schools at the UConn Health campus in Farmington. The University has approximately 10,000 faculty and staff and 32,000 students, including nearly 24,000 undergraduates and over 8,000 graduate and professional students. UConn is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution and is ranked among the top 25 public universities in the nation. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES The successful incumbent will: Develop and implement Extension programs to provide information, education, and technical assistance to community land use decision makers on a wide range of planning topics, including comprehensive planning, open space planning, conducting community resource inventories, economic development, affordable housing, resilience, and roles and responsibilities of land use commissioners.  This work will include, but is not limited to: developing Extension education programs, tools and materials for land use decision makers and other audiences, including workshops (formal and informal), publications, and web information; evaluation of programs; and writing of grant proposals and project reports; Lead the Land Use Academy (LUA), a UConn CLEAR outreach program that focuses on basic and advanced training for land use commissioners; Work with the CT State Office of Policy and Management (OPM), the CT Chapter of the American Planning Association, CT Bar Association, and related agencies to identify and meet the needs of land use commissioners in complying with new mandated land use training requirements; Assist with efforts to connect undergraduate students with outreach to municipalities on land use and resilience issues; Assist in developing and delivering outreach programs focused on natural resource protection, farmland protection and access, housing availability and other pressing issues; Support and enhance access to online training courses, including required training by CT DEEP; and, Integrate the LUA training program with other CLEAR research and outreach programs, with the Connecticut Sea Grant program, and with existing and new partner organizations involved with training local officials. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree in land use planning, natural resources, environmental management, or related discipline; Two years’ professional experience in a field related to land use planning, preferably as a town, regional or consulting planner; Demonstrated experience with municipal land use issues, roles, and responsibilities; Demonstrated experience with the connection between land use activities and sustainability; Demonstrated communication skills, including public speaking and writing of educational materials; Interpersonal skills; Demonstrated experience working as a member of a diverse project team, as well as experience working independently; Experience with standard office word processing, spreadsheet and internet browsing software. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working directly with local land use commissioners or other officials on community planning issues, including economic development, housing, resiliency, and natural resource protection; Experience in developing and delivering effective educational materials, workshops and presentations; AICP certified planner; Experience with land use planning and policy in Connecticut; Demonstrated experience in resiliency planning at the local level; Demonstrated successful experience in grant writing; Experience as funded project director/manager; Experience in teaching; Experience with Geographic Information Systems/geospatial technologies; Experience with Cooperative Extension or similar non-advocacy, research-based, educational programming; Experience with developing online training materials and courses. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a visiting full-time, 11-month, non-tenure track position with an anticipated start date of August 22, 2026. This is currently a grant-funded position with annual review. The successful candidate will work primarily at the University of Connecticut’s Middlesex County extension office located in Haddam, CT, with occasional travel to the Storrs Campus, other extension centers, and elsewhere in the state. The selected incumbent will be required to travel to meeting sites, including some out-of-state travel, and work a flexible schedule, which may include occasional evenings and weekends, to reach target audiences. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499671 and submit the following application materials: A cover letter , Curriculum vitae , Name and Contact information for 3 professional reference s. At the University of Connecticut, our commitment to excellence is complemented by our commitment to building a culturally diverse community. Evaluation of applicants will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Application close: Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Apply now Back to list Refer a friend Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use in Middlesex County Extension Ctr We seek an individual whose professional skills and abilities can provide statewide outreach and training to land use commissioners and others on issues related to land use planning and decision making. This position will lead the award-winning Land Use Academy in the  Center for Land Use Education and Research, advance the Center’s mission of supporting communities in balancing growth and natural resource protection, and have the opportunity to contribute to efforts to connect undergraduates with community extension work. Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
    }
  },
